# CLI verify cycle (local, large work)

After a **large** feature or fix in this **local** environment, the task is not done at build/deploy. Run an Obsidian CLI verify cycle. Skip if there is no local vault/CLI (cloud agent, no `obsidian` on PATH, no `C:\plugin-sandbox-Obsidian\.obsidian\plugins\seek\`).

Large: multi-file behavior, startup/index/search UI, embed/iframe/WebGPU, catch-up/hydrate, anything unit tests cannot see. Not: typo, comment, test-only, docs-only.

## Cycle

1. Follow `.cursor/rules/deploy-and-verify.mdc` (typecheck, relevant tests, build, copy to **sandbox**, reload).
2. Then **runtime CLI verify** against `vault=plugin-sandbox-Obsidian`. Use skills; do not invent a parallel protocol:
   - First-load / hydrate / catch-up / empty search / status labels → `.cursor/skills/seek-cli-startup-debug/SKILL.md` (restart first, serial eval, `dev:debug on` after restart, `dev:console` / `dev:errors`).
   - Deploying a branch into the vault → `.cursor/skills/deploy-branch-to-vault/SKILL.md`.
   - UI/CSS/status-bar/modal/settings proof → `.cursor/skills/seek-visual-verify/SKILL.md` (`capture-surfaces.ps1`).
   - Other runtime: `obsidian eval`, `obsidian seek:search`, `obsidian plugin:reload` as the change requires.
3. Confirm the new behavior (or the bug is gone) from CLI output, not from build success.
4. If CSS/layout/iframe looks stale: try `plugin:reload` first. Use `obsidian restart` only when necessary and **after warning** that it closes every open vault (`.cursor/rules/obsidian-multi-vault-cli.mdc`), then re-probe.

Do not skip because `npm test` passed. Do not probe a warm session when the bug is first-load. Log Seek console lines that matter.

Production vault (`Obsidian`) CLI verify is **not** part of routine task completion — only when the user requests production promotion (see `.cursor/rules/deploy-and-verify.mdc`).
